What is a Variable in UiPath?

A variable is used to store data that can change during the execution of a workflow. It can hold values such as text, 
numbers, files, folders, dates, and more.
A variable is a named storage location used to hold data that can change during the execution of a UiPath workflow.
Variables can store different types of data such as strings, numbers, files, folders, and objects.
Example:

Name = "Harini" (String variable)
Age = 19 (Integer variable)

Variables help you save information and use it later in your automation process.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
How to Create a Variable in UiPath

Method 1: Using Ctrl + K

Select an activity.
Click in the input/output field where you want the variable.
Press Ctrl + K.
Type the variable name and press Enter.

Method 2: Using the Variables Panel

Open the Variables panel at the bottom of the Designer.
Click Create Variable.
Enter the variable name, type, and scope.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

How to Delete a Variable

Method 1: From Variables Panel

Open the Variables panel.
Select the variable.
Right-click and choose Delete.

Method 2: Remove Unused Variables

Go to the Design tab.
Click Remove Unused Variables.
UiPath automatically deletes variables that are not being used.
